  "notes": "USAGE:\nA compound of {提|てい} (present, put forward) + {言|げん} (words). Used as a suru verb ({提言|ていげん}する) to formally propose or recommend. Common in politics, business, and academic contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {提言|ていげん}をまとめる (to compile recommendations)\n- {提言|ていげん}を{行|おこな}う (to make a proposal)\n- {政策|せいさく}{提言|ていげん} (policy recommendation)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {提案|ていあん}: proposal — more general, used in everyday business and conversation\n- {助言|じょげん}: advice — personal guidance rather than formal recommendations",
